---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CTASection from '@/components/CTASection.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '@/lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Green Apple Supplier — Bulk Iranian Green Apples | SibExport"
  description="Green apple supplier from Iran. SibExport supplies fresh Iranian green apples in bulk to importers and wholesale buyers, graded and packed for export. Request a quotation."
  path="/green-apple-export/"
  ogImage="/images/green-apple.png"
>
  <Breadcrumbs
    items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Iranian Apple Varieties', href: '/iranian-apple-varieties/' },
      { label: 'Green Apple Export' },
    ]}
  />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Product"
    title="Green apple supply from Iran"
    description="Fresh, tangy green apples selected for firmness and shelf life — a sharp, distinctive category for your import portfolio."
  />

  <article class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
    <div class="prose-site mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h2>The tart category that completes a program</h2>
      <p>
        Green apples bring something red and golden fruit cannot: acidity.
        Their tart, crisp profile has a loyal following in many markets, and
        for importers they serve a useful commercial role — differentiating a
        product range and appealing to customers who find sweeter apples
        ordinary. In mixed wholesale programs, a reliable green category
        alongside red and golden fruit signals a supplier who can serve the
        whole market rather than part of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        SibExport supplies green apples from Iranian orchards in export
        volumes, graded and packed against a written specification. As with
        every category we ship, the specification is agreed with you before
        sourcing begins — variety, size count, grade and packing are all
        confirmed in writing.
      </p>

      <h3>Characteristics buyers care about</h3>

    <figure class="my-8">
      <img
        src="/images/green-apple.svg"
        alt="Firm green apples selected for export"
        width="1200"
        height="630"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full rounded-xl border border-border shadow-sm"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-muted-foreground">Firm green apples selected for export</figcaption>
    </figure>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Acidity and flavor</strong> — the tart brightness that
          defines the category and drives repeat purchase among its fans
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Firmness</strong> — green apples are typically among the
          firmest fruit in a program, which suits them to handling and
          longer transit
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Color</strong> — the bright, uniform green without
          excessive yellowing that signals freshness in the category
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Shelf behavior</strong> — firmer, more acidic fruit
          generally holds eating quality longer, a practical advantage for
          distributors
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Varieties and general market information</h3>
      <p>
        Internationally, the green category is dominated by Granny Smith and
        similar tart varieties. Iran's orchards grow a range of green-type
        apples suited to wholesale trade. A clear distinction matters here:
        general information about green apple categories is widely known, but
        <strong>what SibExport can actually supply in a given season is a
        separate question</strong> — one we answer per order, in writing,
        against your specification. We do not publish a fixed variety list
        because availability genuinely changes with harvest and storage
        cycles.
      </p>

      <h3>Size counts and grading</h3>
      <p>
        Green apples for export follow the same sizing logic as other
        categories: count per carton defines fruit size, and the grade sets
        tolerances for color, firmness and surface defects. Because the
        category is often bought alongside red and golden fruit, buyers
        frequently align counts across all three classes. Send us the count
        and grade your market expects — or your current specification sheet —
        and we will confirm what Iranian supply can match.
      </p>

      <h3>Packing, storage and transportation</h3>
      <p>
        Green apples' firmness makes them a robust shipping category, but
        that is not a reason to relax packing standards. Fruit ships in
        export-grade cartons with interior packaging matched to the journey's
        length and conditions, and cold-chain handling from packing to
        loading follows the same discipline as the rest of our program. For
        regional road-freight destinations — Iraq, the Caucasus, Turkey, the
        Gulf — short transit works strongly in favor of arrival condition.
      </p>
      <p>
        Packing options and confirmation workflow are covered on the
        <a href="/apple-packaging/">apple packaging</a> page; the inspection
        points that protect quality are described under
        <a href="/apple-quality-specifications/">quality and specifications</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Who this supply suits</h3>
      <p>
        Bulk green apples from Iran suit importers completing a three-color
        program, wholesalers serving markets where tart apples outsell sweet
        ones, and food distributors looking for firm fruit that tolerates
        demanding distribution chains. If green apples are a gap in your
        current range, or your existing supply is inconsistent, request a
        quotation with your specification and destination — we will respond
        with a realistic offer.
      </p>

      <h3>Frequently asked questions about green apple supply</h3>
      <p><strong>Can I buy Iranian green apples in bulk?</strong><br />
      Yes. SibExport supplies the green category in export volumes alongside
      red and golden apples. Volume minimums are confirmed per order.</p>
      <p><strong>Which green varieties do you supply?</strong><br />
      Variety availability changes with the season. Tell us the profile your
      market expects — tartness, size, color — and we will confirm in writing
      what the current crop can deliver.</p>
      <p><strong>Do green apples ship as well as red?</strong><br />
      Green apples are typically firm and travel well, particularly by road
      to regional destinations. Packing and cold-chain handling still follow
      full export standards.</p>
      <p><strong>How do I start?</strong><br />
      Send your specification and destination through the quotation form or
      WhatsApp. The more detail you provide, the more precise the offer.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <CTASection
    title="Ready to add Iranian green apples to your program?"
    description={`Send your sizes, grades, volume and destination — via the quotation form or WhatsApp at ${CONTACT.whatsappInternational}.`}
  />
</BaseLayout>
